得了吧。

618
00:28:34.180 --> 00:28:35.940
You're bringing up her side ponytail.
你提到了她的侧马尾。

619
00:28:35.940 --> 00:28:37.160
What about her bangs?
那她的刘海呢？

620
00:28:37.500 --> 00:28:39.260
I mean, she has bangs.
我是说，她有刘海。

621
00:28:39.500 --> 00:28:44.560
She has bangs, but she has an extension-filled side ponytail.
她有刘海，但她扎了个接发侧马尾。

622
00:28:45.140 --> 00:28:46.680
There's a lot happening with her hair.
她的头发很有戏。

623
00:28:46.840 --> 00:28:49.720
I don't have a sting for it, but it would go full Mindy.
我没有专门的音效，但那绝对是典型的明迪风格。

624
00:28:50.620 --> 00:28:51.060
Yeah.
是啊。

625
00:28:51.420 --> 00:28:53.140
Why don't we have a full Mindy sting?
我们为什么没有一个完整的明迪音效？

626
00:28:53.220 --> 00:28:54.340
We really need to get on that.
我们真的得弄一个。

627
00:28:54.340 --> 00:28:54.560
I don't know.
我不知道。

628
00:28:54.560 --> 00:28:55.780
Someone make us a full Mindy sting.
谁给我们做一个完整的明迪音效吧。

629
00:28:55.900 --> 00:28:56.500
Someone do it.
谁来做一下。

630
00:28:56.840 --> 00:29:00.920
Well, this leads to a very famous office line.
好吧，这引出了一句非常著名的办公室台词。

631
00:29:01.300 --> 00:29:02.080
Fashion show.
时装秀。

632
00:29:02.240 --> 00:29:02.940
Fashion show.
时装秀。

633
00:29:03.080 --> 00:29:04.400
Fashion show at lunch.
午餐时装秀。

634
00:29:05.100 --> 00:29:05.540
Yes.
没错。

635
00:29:06.240 --> 00:29:06.760
Yes.
没错。

636
00:29:07.020 --> 00:29:09.440
Guys, that is 100% scripted.
伙计们，那百分之百是剧本写的。

637
00:29:09.580 --> 00:29:10.620
That was in the script.
那是剧本里的内容。

638
00:29:10.740 --> 00:29:11.600
That was not an improv.
那不是即兴发挥。

639
00:29:12.120 --> 00:29:14.680
It was written exactly like that.
剧本里就是那样写的。

640
00:29:15.120 --> 00:29:16.580
Mindy delivers it perfectly.
明迪演绎得非常完美。

641
00:29:17.100 --> 00:29:19.700
We had a lot of fan questions about this scene.
我们收到了很多粉丝关于这个场景的问题。

642
00:29:19.940 --> 00:29:25.540
People mostly wanted to know, did I get to pick out the outfits that Pam gets in her online
大家最想知道的是，帕姆在网购狂欢中买的衣服是我挑的吗？

643
00:29:25.540 --> 00:29:26.540
shopping spree?
还有，盒子里除了她后来在厨房里拿出来穿的那件衬衫外，还有别的东西吗？

644
00:29:26.540 --> 00:29:31.400
And also, were there more things in the box besides that single shirt that she gets out
好的，是的。

645
00:29:31.400 --> 00:29:32.760
and wears later in the kitchen?
我们专门试装讨论过这些衣服应该是什么样的。

646
00:29:33.220 --> 00:29:34.220
Okay, yes.
盒子里确实还有别的东西。

647
00:29:34.440 --> 00:29:39.040
We had a big wardrobe fitting about what would these outfits be.
但我得告诉你，它们基本上都是同一款衬衫，不过有一件是绿松石色的。

648
00:29:39.040 --> 00:29:41.920
And there were more things in the box.
那里面有很多宝石色调的衬衫，看起来和你看到的那件衬衫几乎一模一样。

649
00:29:42.080 --> 00:29:47.900
But I'll have to tell you, they were basically that same shirt, but there was a turquoise one.
它们基本上都是同一款衬衫，不过有一件是绿松石色的。

650
00:29:48.340 --> 00:29:55.260
It was a lot of jewel-toned shirts that looked almost identical to that one shirt that you see.
那里面有很多宝石色调的衬衫，看起来和你看到的那件衬衫几乎一模一样。

651
00:29:55.260 --> 00:29:56.940
And that was kind of part of the joke.
那其实也是笑话的一部分。

652
00:29:57.100 --> 00:29:58.860
Because have you done that when you're shopping?
因为你在购物的时候有没有过这种情况？

653
00:29:58.860 --> 00:30:00.860
You're like, I'm going to get a whole new wardrobe.
你会想，我要买一整套全新的行头。

654
00:30:00.860 --> 00:30:05.580
And then you just kind of go to the store and buy the same pair of pants in three colors.
然后你到了店里，结果买了三条同款不同色的裤子。

655
00:30:05.900 --> 00:30:06.440
Oh, my gosh.
天哪。

656
00:30:06.440 --> 00:30:07.200
I always do that.
我总是这样。

657
00:30:07.300 --> 00:30:10.260
I find, like, one shirt I like and then buy it in three colors.
我发现一件喜欢的衬衫，就会买下三种颜色。

658
00:30:10.420 --> 00:30:13.020
And people are like, hey, I – oh, have you worn that?
然后别人会说，嘿，我——哦，你穿过那件吗？

659
00:30:13.120 --> 00:30:15.740
Oh, I – is that a – and I'm like, no, it's the same shirt.
哦，我——那是——我会说，不，那是同一件衬衫。

660
00:30:15.800 --> 00:30:16.380
It's the same shirt.
那是同一件衬衫。

661
00:30:16.380 --> 00:30:20.460
Yeah, that was kind of what happened with Pam's, like,
没错，帕姆的情况也差不多，就像，

662
00:30:20.780 --> 00:30:28.460
redesign of her wardrobe was that she managed to find one thing that she was willing to take a chance on and then bought it in different colors.
她重新设计自己的衣橱时，就是设法找到了一件她愿意尝试的衣服，然后买了不同颜色的。

663
00:30:28.900 --> 00:30:30.640
Here's what I remember about that, Jenna.
关于那件事，我记得是这样的，珍娜。

664
00:30:30.920 --> 00:30:35.580
Because all of us saw each other every day pretty much in the same wardrobe, right?
因为我们几乎每天都能看到彼此穿着同样的衣服，对吧？

665
00:30:35.820 --> 00:30:36.060
Yeah.
是的。

666
00:30:36.380 --> 00:30:40.960
Whenever one of our characters did get anything slightly different, we were like, hey.
每当我们的角色穿了稍微不同的衣服，我们就会说，嘿。

667
00:30:40.960 --> 00:30:41.280
Yay.
耶。

668
00:30:42.100 --> 00:30:50.480
So, I remember our reactions to your red fancy blouse so similar to our characters, minus the gross pervy stuff.
所以我记得我们对你那件红色时髦衬衫的反应，和我们的角色非常像，只不过少了那些恶心猥琐的部分。

669
00:30:50.720 --> 00:30:53.120
But we were all like, oh, my God, you look so great.
但我们当时都说，天哪，你看上去太棒了。

670
00:30:53.220 --> 00:30:54.320
Oh, my God, you look amazing.
天哪，你看上去美极了。

671
00:30:55.100 --> 00:30:58.360
And you're like, oh, it's just the wardrobe or the scene.
而你会说，哦，那只是戏服或者剧情需要。

672
00:30:59.820 --> 00:31:05.640
It did feel like that whenever we got a slightly fancier hairdo or a slightly cooler outfit.
每当我们换了稍微好看点的发型或者穿了稍微酷点的衣服，感觉确实就是那样。

673
00:31:06.280 --> 00:31:06.700
Yeah.
没错。

674
00:31:07.160 --> 00:31:08.080
Everyone noticed.
每个人都注意到了。

675
00:31:08.460 --> 00:31:08.900
Cast and crew.
演员和剧组人员。

676
00:31:08.900 --> 00:31:09.800
We all talked about it.
我们都讨论过。

677
00:31:09.800 --> 00:31:11.160
We were like, wow, look at that.
我们当时说，哇，看那个。

678
00:31:11.280 --> 00:31:11.540
Wow.
哇。

679
00:31:13.140 --> 00:31:15.480
So, now we're back at Stanford, m'lady.
好了，现在我们回到斯坦福分部了，女士。

680
00:31:16.200 --> 00:31:17.120
Back at Stanford.
回到斯坦福。

681
00:31:17.400 --> 00:31:23.120
And Andy is getting ticked off at Jim for killing the wrong soldiers in Call of Duty.
安迪因为吉姆在《使命召唤》里杀错了士兵而感到恼火。

682
00:31:24.000 --> 00:31:24.500
Yes.
是的。

683
00:31:24.620 --> 00:31:30.780
And did you notice at 4 minutes and 59 seconds, there is still a blue sticky note on Jim's computer that says, smile?
你有没有注意到在4分59秒的时候，吉姆的电脑上还有一张写着“微笑”的蓝色便利贴？

684
00:31:31.260 --> 00:31:32.660
No, I didn't notice.
不，我没注意到。

685
00:31:32.820 --> 00:31:33.700
That was a great catch.
你观察得真仔细。

686
00:31:34.040 --> 00:31:35.500
Yeah, it's still there.
没错，它还在那儿。

687
00:31:35.500 --> 00:31:37.540
Fan question from Shelby Hagen.
来自谢尔比·黑根的粉丝提问。

688
00:31:37.760 --> 00:31:42.460
How was Call of Duty chosen as the game that was played in the Stanford branch?
《使命召唤》是怎么被选为斯坦福分部里玩的游戏的？

689
00:31:42.460 --> 00:31:45.320
Thank you so much for your question, Shelby.
非常感谢你的提问，谢尔比。

690
00:31:45.580 --> 00:31:51.120
We actually got so many questions about Call of Duty, and this seemed like the perfect one to get us started.
我们确实收到了很多关于《使命召唤》的问题，这看起来是个完美的开场问题。

691
00:31:51.400 --> 00:31:55.360
As you guys know, Jenna and I were not in those scenes at Stanford.
如你们所知，珍娜和我当时并没有参与斯坦福的那些场景。

692
00:31:55.360 --> 00:31:56.600
That's right.
没错。

693
00:31:57.000 --> 00:32:02.980
So, Shelby, I reached out to a lot of people to get you the real deal on all things Call of Duty.
所以，谢尔比，我联系了很多人，为了给你带来关于《使命召唤》的一切真相。

694
00:32:03.300 --> 00:32:06.940
Angela, I got all the scoop from our line producer, Kent Sabornak.
安吉拉，我从我们的制片主任肯特·萨博纳克那里得到了所有内幕。

695
00:32:07.280 --> 00:32:12.860
I texted with our editor, Dean Holland, and Andy Bernard himself, Ed HelMs.
我给我们的剪辑师迪恩·霍兰德，还有安迪·伯纳德本人，也就是艾德·赫尔姆斯发了短信。

696
00:32:13.080 --> 00:32:15.300
Lainey, that is a serious deep dive.
莱妮，这真是深度挖掘啊。

697
00:32:15.440 --> 00:32:15.940
I like it.
我喜欢。

698
00:32:16.000 --> 00:32:16.580
I like it.
我喜欢。

699
00:32:16.700 --> 00:32:17.660
I deep dived.
我进行了深度挖掘。

700
00:32:17.780 --> 00:32:18.540
I really did.
我确实做了。

701
00:32:18.720 --> 00:32:19.780
Okay, so what did you find out?
好的，那你查到了什么？

702
00:32:19.780 --> 00:32:29.060
All right, so Kent told me that after we wrapped season one of the show, the post-production guys moved to some offices in Venice to edit the episodes.
行，肯特告诉我，在我们拍完第一季后，后期制作团队搬到了威尼斯的一些办公室去剪辑剧集。

703
00:32:29.360 --> 00:32:41.120
And while they were there, Kent, just for whatever reason, just on a whim, installed Call of Duty on everyone's computers, just so they could blow off steam during edit sessions.
当他们在那里的时候，肯特不知出于什么原因，心血来潮在每个人的电脑上都装了《使命召唤》，好让他们在剪辑间隙放松一下。

704
00:32:41.120 --> 00:32:50.880
And then when we moved to our new stages for season two, he did it again, but this time he also installed it on all of the writers' computers.
后来我们搬到第二季的新摄影棚时，他又如法炮制，但这次他还给所有编剧的电脑也都装上了。

705
00:32:50.920 --> 00:32:56.020
And that is when the editors and the writers started playing one another.
也就是从那时起，剪辑师和编剧们开始互相切磋了。

706
00:32:56.220 --> 00:32:59.840
I remember this because our editors and writers were in the same building.
我记得很清楚，因为当时我们的剪辑师和编剧都在同一栋楼里。

707
00:33:00.120 --> 00:33:01.840
They were over where the warehouse is, right?
他们就在仓库那边，对吧？

708
00:33:02.080 --> 00:33:04.560
And the writers were upstairs and the editors were downstairs.
编剧在楼上，剪辑师在楼下。

709
00:33:04.560 --> 00:33:09.880
And sometimes I would go over there at lunch because I was friends with Claire Scanlon, one of our editors at the time.
有时候我会去那边吃午饭，因为我和当时的剪辑师之一克莱尔·斯坎伦是朋友。

710
00:33:10.040 --> 00:33:14.300
And I would walk in the editing bay and they were all like, get down!
我走进剪辑室时，他们全都喊着：趴下！

711
00:33:14.580 --> 00:33:15.340
Over here!
这边！

712
00:33:15.640 --> 00:33:16.960
I was like, what is happening?
我当时心想，这是在干嘛？

713
00:33:18.460 --> 00:33:21.860
I remember going up to the writers' room and seeing the same thing.
我记得去编剧室时也看到了同样的情景。

714
00:33:22.040 --> 00:33:27.920
They had this big conference table in the writers' room and they would have all their computers in a circle.
编剧室里有一张大会议桌，他们把所有电脑围成一圈摆放。

715
00:33:27.920 --> 00:33:34.240
And then some people had little offices and then some people would be around this conference room table.
有些人有独立办公室，有些人就围坐在会议桌旁。

716
00:33:34.440 --> 00:33:35.480
And it was the same thing.
情况是一样的。

717
00:33:35.640 --> 00:33:37.480
They did exactly like what Stanford did.
他们做得和斯坦福分部的一模一样。

718
00:33:37.560 --> 00:33:38.820
They would turn off the lights.
他们会关掉灯。

719
00:33:38.820 --> 00:33:39.080
Yeah.
没错。

720
00:33:39.360 --> 00:33:42.740
And they would have this elaborate match going on.
然后进行一场精心策划的对战。

721
00:33:42.880 --> 00:33:44.460
Oh my gosh, they were so into it.
天哪，他们太投入了。

722
00:33:44.780 --> 00:33:47.980
Well, I guess Greg Daniels was particularly obsessed.
我想格雷格·丹尼尔斯尤其沉迷其中。

723
00:33:47.980 --> 00:33:57.920
In fact, our editor, Dean Holland, told me that the very first time he met with Greg to start editing an episode, within about 10 minutes, Greg said,
事实上，我们的剪辑师迪恩·霍兰德告诉我，他第一次和格雷格见面商讨剪辑剧集时，不到10分钟，格雷格就问：

724
00:33:58.600 --> 00:33:59.840
have you ever played Call of Duty?
你玩过《使命召唤》吗？

725
00:34:00.280 --> 00:34:01.700
And Dean was like, yeah.
迪恩说，玩过。

726
00:34:02.220 --> 00:34:05.320
And he said, Greg left the room and started a 20-person game.
他说，格雷格当时就离开了房间，发起了一场20人的游戏。

727
00:34:06.280 --> 00:34:07.820
Like within 10 minutes.
就在10分钟之内。

728
00:34:08.240 --> 00:34:12.560
How perfect that Greg was the person that directed this episode because he loves Call of Duty.
格雷格来执导这一集真是太完美了，因为他超爱《使命召唤》。

729
00:34:12.820 --> 00:34:13.460
I know.
我知道。

730
00:34:13.580 --> 00:34:14.100
He loves it.
他太爱了。

731
00:34:14.200 --> 00:34:16.020
I don't think that was a mistake.
我觉得这绝非巧合。

732
00:34:16.880 --> 00:34:17.360
No.
没错。

733
00:34:17.980 --> 00:34:18.360
No.
确实。

734
00:34:18.780 --> 00:34:19.260
All right.
好吧。

735
00:34:19.340 --> 00:34:22.080
Well, I have a little runner-up question for you, Jenna.
那么，珍娜，我还有一个小小的后续问题要问你。

736
00:34:22.720 --> 00:34:22.960
Okay.
好的。

737
00:34:23.240 --> 00:34:26.980
So Evan Warburton wrote in and said, hey, I need to point this out.
埃文·沃伯顿写信来说，嘿，我得指出这一点。

738
00:34:27.440 --> 00:34:31.840
Jim is apparently horrible at Call of Duty at the Stanford branch in this episode.
在这一集中，吉姆在斯坦福分部玩《使命召唤》的技术显然烂透了。

739
00:34:32.140 --> 00:34:42.640
But in the episode email surveillance, you can see in the background of the scene at 20 minutes, 8 seconds, that Toby is playing Call of Duty on Jim's TV.
但在《邮件监控》那一集中，你可以看到在20分08秒的背景画面里，托比正在吉姆的电视上玩《使命召唤》。

740
00:34:43.160 --> 00:34:44.540
Remember at the barbecue, Jenna?
还记得烧烤派对那次吗，珍娜？

741
00:34:44.640 --> 00:34:45.000
Yes.
记得。

742
00:34:45.120 --> 00:34:45.340
Okay.
好的。

743
00:34:45.500 --> 00:34:45.660
Yes.
是的。

744
00:34:45.660 --> 00:34:54.640
So, and then also in Jim's bedroom at 15 minutes, 52 seconds, you can see an expansion pack of Call of Duty on Jim's desk.
还有，在吉姆卧室的15分52秒处，你可以看到吉姆的桌子上放着《使命召唤》的扩展包。

745
00:34:54.840 --> 00:34:55.500
Come on.
得了吧。

746
00:34:55.660 --> 00:34:56.620
Someone please explain.
谁来解释一下。

747
00:34:57.260 --> 00:34:57.760
All right.
好的。

748
00:34:57.900 --> 00:34:58.240
Yes.
是的。

749
00:34:58.240 --> 00:35:01.100
We actually had a lot of people write in about this glitch.
其实很多人都写信来问过这个漏洞。

750
00:35:01.100 --> 00:35:04.240
I went to that time code, 15 minutes, 52 seconds.
我特意去看了那个时间点，15分52秒。

751
00:35:04.620 --> 00:35:05.520
There it is.
就是这个。

752
00:35:05.660 --> 00:35:07.540
There is an expansion pack Call of Duty.
《使命召唤》有个资料片。

753
00:35:08.400 --> 00:35:09.980
Here's how this went down, guys.
事情是这样的，伙计们。

754
00:35:10.360 --> 00:35:10.460
Okay.
好的。

755
00:35:10.620 --> 00:35:19.360
Kent told me that the writers had a card up on the wall in the writer's room all through season two about a possible Call of Duty storyline.
肯特告诉我，编剧室的墙上在第二季期间一直贴着一张卡片，上面写着一个可能的《使命召唤》剧情线。

756
00:35:19.360 --> 00:35:22.080
But they couldn't really ever figure out how to put it in.
但他们一直没想好该怎么把它加进去。

757
00:35:22.180 --> 00:35:25.680
And they had originally thought about doing something in email surveillance.
他们最初想过在“邮件监控”那一集里做点文章。

758
00:35:26.420 --> 00:35:34.540
And if you remember, Angela, we did actually shoot some scenes where people were playing Call of Duty during Jim's party.
安吉拉，如果你还记得的话，我们确实拍了一些吉姆派对上大家玩《使命召唤》的镜头。

759
00:35:34.840 --> 00:35:35.020
Yeah.
没错。

760
00:35:35.020 --> 00:35:36.680
But it wasn't a storyline.
但那不是一条剧情线。

761
00:35:37.140 --> 00:35:37.260
Yeah.
